Change in displacement: $\Delta x=11-6=5\text{ m}$, to the right.

Distance travelled: $|2-6|+|11-2|=4+9=13\text{ m}$.

Split the journey at each reversal and add the lengths. If velocity keeps the same sign throughout an interval, distance travelled is simply the magnitude of the change in displacement.
